Supabase on AWS

Gateway configuration is adapted from Supabase self-hosted/v0.8.3:
https://github.com/supabase/supabase/tree/self-hosted/v0.8.3/docker/volumes/api/envoy
Copyright its respective contributors. Licensed under Apache License 2.0.
Modifications remove unused/public administration routes, adapt private DNS,
trust the ALB forwarding hop, and omit sensitive URL fields from access logs.

Key generation follows the same release's docker/utils/add-new-auth-keys.sh.

Database prerequisites and schema-cache triggers are adapted from Supabase Postgres 17.6.1.136:
https://github.com/supabase/postgres/tree/17.6.1.136/migrations/db
Licensed under the PostgreSQL License, reproduced below.
Modifications retain only Auth, REST and Storage prerequisites, validate baseline
adoption, and use RDS-compatible administration. Distribution superuser changes,
preload libraries, platform roles and excluded components' migrations are omitted.
Auth and Storage retain their own unmodified schema migrations.

Architecture inspired by supabase-community/supabase-on-aws (Apache-2.0).
https://github.com/supabase-community/supabase-on-aws

